WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.394
Welcome to Section Five: Leading.

2
00:00:02.594 --> 00:00:06.532
Human resources systems help people enter and develop in their roles.

3
00:00:06.732 --> 00:00:11.773
Leading concerns how people are guided, motivated, and supported in everyday work.

4
00:00:11.973 --> 00:00:20.723
At our fictional Cedar Crossing Library, a small project group is preparing a community history display with photographs, audio clips, and written captions.

5
00:00:20.923 --> 00:00:24.017
The staff bring different experience and different concerns.

6
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:28.225
Producing a useful display will require more than assigning tasks.

7
00:00:28.425 --> 00:00:34.784
We will examine motivation, leadership, ethics, communication, and teamwork through this invented project.

8
00:00:34.984 --> 00:00:42.278
The recurring diagram asks us to understand people, guide the work, judge fairly, communicate, and empower with review.

9
00:00:42.478 --> 00:00:45.833
These are connected questions, not a fixed textbook formula.

10
00:00:46.033 --> 00:00:49.461
The assessed Self-Managed Team Experiment is a separate case.

11
00:00:49.661 --> 00:00:53.442
This optional lesson supports Chapters Thirteen through Seventeen.

12
00:00:53.642 --> 00:00:56.779
You can listen, read, revisit, or skip practice.

13
00:00:56.979 --> 00:01:01.564
Your last chapter is remembered on this browser; nothing is submitted to Canvas.
